## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to add A/B rollout gating to privacy-preserving analytics, determinism, offline behavior, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Deterministic variant assignment from masked ID and locale
- Privacy: no exposure of raw IDs
- Offline handling and rollback
- Observability and tests

```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function selectVariant(userIdMasked, locale, salt) {
  const data = userIdMasked + '|' + locale + '|' + salt;
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(data).digest('hex');
  return (parseInt(hash.substring(0,8), 16) % 2) ? 'v2' : 'v1';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to multiple concurrent experiments?
- How would you validate privacy guarantees in tests?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of reproducibility, determinism, and data lineage in a beginner-friendly setting. Emphasizes auditability and simple tests.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic feature engineering
- Data lineage and reproducibility IDs
- Minimal, auditable API design
- Lightweight explainability vectors

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function computeReproScore(userId, region, modelVersion, seed) {
  const input = `${userId}|${region}|${modelVersion}|${seed}`;
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(input).digest('hex');
  const n = parseInt(hash.slice(0, 8), 16);
  return (n % 1000) / 10; // deterministic score 0-99.9
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in reproducibility across model_version updates?
- How would you secure seeds and input digests to protect privacy while enabling audits?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design consent-aware data pipelines and enforce privacy rules in a concrete API.

## Key Concepts
- Field-level consent
- RBAC and policy enforcement
- Auditability and traceability

## Code Example
```javascript
function applyConsent(userConsent, payload){
  const result={};
  if(userConsent.region) result.region=payload.region;
  if(userConsent.locale) result.locale=payload.locale;
  if(userConsent.model_version) result.model_version=payload.model_version;
  return result;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model consent changes over time for existing users?
- How would you test RBAC boundaries in CI?

## Why This Is Asked

Explores secure aggregation with tamper-evident provenance and differential privacy in a multi-tenant setup, a realistic requirement for enterprise customers.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving aggregation (MPC/HE/DP)
- Tamper-evident provenance (Merkle/dag)
- Nonce/replay protection and versioned schemas
- Per-tenant privacy budgets and audits

## Code Example

